Personally, I see competition merely as a tool, not something I have any
interest in for its own sake.  While it is one factor in forcing people to
strive for better things, and a very powerful one, it is not the only one. 
Another is simply the desire for a better life, be it for oneself or for
everyone.  Both in the current world and in the above stagnant dystopia, most
people work largely at what I consider to be meaningless chores --
manufacturing articles of daily life like clothes, cars, and food, carrying
these things from place to place, and disposing of the resulting waste.  Never
mind uploading, nanotech, and the rest -- what I would *really* like in the
nearer future is never to have to brush my teeth, do the laundry, maintain my
house and garden, change the batteries in my radio, shop for groceries, or a
hundred other items of petty drudgery, still less spend a large part of my
waking hours doing any of these things for other people, however good the pay.

